[8.444744, "o", "--- ROUTE ---\r\n"]
[8.448714, "o", "tarnpit\r\nhopcue\r\nwatchbay\r\n"]
[8.449112, "o", "--- VERBS ---\r\n"]
[8.449969, "o", "kindle\r\n  rebuild ship.jar and draft.jar from current sources\r\n\r\nwatch BAG\r\n  run the ship mill on BAG and write /app/jarhearth/watch.json\r\n\r\npeek BAG\r\n  print the gather word for BAG as one integer on stdout\r\n\r\ndraft BAG\r\n  run the draft mill on BAG\r\n"]
[8.451388, "o", "--- CARD ---\r\n"]
[8.452449, "o", "watch.json object:\r\n  seen  — integer gather word the mill stored\r\n  bag   — basename of the bag path\r\n  note  — same basename\r\n\r\nThe gather word for a published bag is the wait-board integer the gatherer publishes after it reads the bag.\r\nThat integer is not the bag's first-line token alone.\r\nA first line of 0 means the gatherer never publishes.\r\nShipped sample bags: `/app/hopbags/elm.bag`, `/app/hopbags/mute.bag`. Grade-time bags may appear as `/app/hopbags/held.bag`, `/app/hopbags/held2.bag`, `/app/hopbags/side.bag`.\r\n"]
[8.452766, "o", "--- MARK ---\r\n"]
[8.453656, "o", "keld-tight-9\r\n"]
[8.453855, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@9191728e3ef4:/app# "]
[8.570731, "i", "printf '%s\\n' '--- TREE ---'; find /app -maxdepth 4 -type f -printf '%p\\n' | sort\n"]
[8.571292, "o", "printf '%s\\n' '--- TREE ---'; find /app -maxdepth 4 -type f -printf '%p\\n' | sort\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r--- TREE ---\r\n"]
